praṇaṣṭas te dhanañ-jaya\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":4863,\"bb\":4253,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/72/b4253/\",\"shadow_value\":\"kaccit – whether; etat – this; śrutam – heard; pārtha – O son of Pṛthā; tvayā – by you; eka-agreṇa – with full attention; cetasā – by the mind; kaccit – whether; ajñāna – of ignorance; sammohaḥ – the illusion; praṇaṣṭaḥ – dispelled; te – of you; dhanam-jaya – O conqueror of wealth (Arjuna).\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"kaccit\",\"translation\":\"whether\"},{\"word\":\"etat\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"śrutam\",\"translation\":\"heard\"},{\"word\":\"pārtha\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pṛthā\"},{\"word\":\"tvayā\",\"translation\":\"by you\"},{\"word\":\"eka-agreṇa\",\"translation\":\"with full attention\"},{\"word\":\"cetasā\",\"translation\":\"by the mind\"},{\"word\":\"kaccit\",\"translation\":\"whether\"},{\"word\":\"ajñāna\",\"translation\":\"of ignorance\"},{\"word\":\"sammohaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the illusion\"},{\"word\":\"praṇaṣṭaḥ\",\"translation\":\"dispelled\"},{\"word\":\"te\",\"translation\":\"of you\"},{\"word\":\"dhanam-jaya\",\"translation\":\"O conqueror of wealth (Arjuna)\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":4864,\"bb\":4254,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/72/b4254/\",\"body_value\":\"O son of Pṛthā, O conqueror of wealth, have you heard this with an attentive mind? And are your ignorance and illusions now dispelled?\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4865,\"bb\":4255,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/72/b4255/\",\"body_value\":\"The Lord was acting as the spiritual master of Arjuna. Therefore it was His duty to inquire from Arjuna whether he understood the whole Bhagavad-gītā in its proper perspective. If not, the Lord was ready to re-explain any point, or the whole Bhagavad-gītā if so required. Actually, anyone who hears Bhagavad-gītā from a bona fide spiritual master like Kṛṣṇa or His representative will find that all his ignorance is dispelled. Bhagavad-gītā is not an ordinary book written by a poet or fiction writer; it is spoken by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Any person fortunate enough to hear these teachings from Kṛṣṇa or from His bona fide spiritual representative is sure to become a liberated person and get out of the darkness of ignorance.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 18.72\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 18.72\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"29:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n2f:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n25:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/